1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:03,550
Snippets, and reusable content.

2
00:00:04,350 --> 00:00:07,008
A team member does not have a URL.

3
00:00:07,008 --> 00:00:11,152
A testimonial does not have a place in the page tree.

4
00:00:11,152 --> 00:00:15,843
But both belong on pages, and usually on more than one page.

5
00:00:15,843 --> 00:00:17,875
That is what a snippet is.

6
00:00:17,875 --> 00:00:22,488
A plain Django model, that editors can manage in the admin.

7
00:00:23,288 --> 00:00:24,138
Two models.

8
00:00:24,138 --> 00:00:26,689
A team member, and a testimonial.

9
00:00:26,689 --> 00:00:29,085
Neither one inherits from Page.

10
00:00:29,085 --> 00:00:34,650
The team member inherits from Orderable, which adds a sort order column,

11
00:00:34,650 --> 00:00:38,978
and that alone gives the admin drag and drop reordering.

12
00:00:39,778 --> 00:00:45,126
And you register them with a snippet view set, which is the Wagtail seven way.

13
00:00:45,126 --> 00:00:48,554
One class per model sets the icon, the menu label,

14
00:00:48,554 --> 00:00:51,502
the listing columns and what is searchable.

15
00:00:51,502 --> 00:00:56,987
A view set group puts both of them under a single Studio item in the admin menu,

16
00:00:56,987 --> 00:01:00,484
instead of burying them in a generic snippets list.

17
00:01:01,284 --> 00:01:04,484
There are two ways to put a snippet on a page.

18
00:01:04,484 --> 00:01:06,572
Either the editor chooses one,

19
00:01:06,572 --> 00:01:11,024
which is what the testimonial block does with a snippet chooser.

20
00:01:11,024 --> 00:01:13,320
Or the block fetches them itself.

21
00:01:13,320 --> 00:01:15,894
The team block has nothing to choose.

22
00:01:15,894 --> 00:01:20,208
It loads every team member, so when somebody joins the studio,

23
00:01:20,208 --> 00:01:23,478
every page showing the team updates on its own.

24
00:01:24,278 --> 00:01:30,155
Blocks have a get context method as well, exactly like pages did last episode.

25
00:01:30,155 --> 00:01:35,504
And notice the import is inside the method, not at the top of the file.

26
00:01:36,304 --> 00:01:41,395
Because the models file imports the blocks file, to build the body field.

27
00:01:41,395 --> 00:01:44,812
If the blocks file imported the models file back,

28
00:01:44,812 --> 00:01:48,438
that is a circular import and Django will not start.

29
00:01:48,438 --> 00:01:51,995
So the snippet chooser names its model as a string,

30
00:01:51,995 --> 00:01:56,458
and the team block imports its model only when it actually runs.

31
00:01:57,258 --> 00:02:02,661
Now, what happens when somebody deletes a testimonial that a page is using.

32
00:02:02,661 --> 00:02:05,615
Before the delete, Wagtail already knows.

33
00:02:05,615 --> 00:02:09,721
Its reference index says used one time, on the home page,

34
00:02:09,721 --> 00:02:13,467
and the admin shows that on the confirmation screen.

35
00:02:13,467 --> 00:02:16,277
After the delete, the page still loads.

36
00:02:16,277 --> 00:02:18,726
But the block's value is now None,

37
00:02:18,726 --> 00:02:23,913
and without a guard in the template you ship an empty, styled quote box.

38
00:02:23,913 --> 00:02:26,507
Every chooser value can become None.

39
00:02:26,507 --> 00:02:28,380
Write the template for it.

40
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,904
Now tags for the journal.

41
00:02:30,904 --> 00:02:34,905
A small through model, and a taggable manager on the post.

42
00:02:34,905 --> 00:02:39,251
The detail that matters is parental key instead of foreign key.

43
00:02:39,251 --> 00:02:43,321
It means the tags are saved as part of the page's revision,

44
00:02:43,321 --> 00:02:48,494
so an editor can change the tags on a draft without touching the live post.

45
00:02:49,294 --> 00:02:53,129
Filtering by tag is four lines in get context.

46
00:02:53,129 --> 00:02:58,632
And the last of those four lines matters a lot more than it looks.

47
00:02:58,632 --> 00:02:59,632
Here is why.

48
00:03:00,432 --> 00:03:02,710
Filter by the process tag.

49
00:03:02,710 --> 00:03:04,112
Page one of two.

50
00:03:04,112 --> 00:03:05,163
Click older.

51
00:03:05,163 --> 00:03:11,910
The link is question mark page equals two, and it lands on page two of three.

52
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:14,626
That is the unfiltered journal.

53
00:03:14,626 --> 00:03:16,554
The tag just vanished.

54
00:03:17,354 --> 00:03:21,830
Last episode's pagination links replace the entire query string.

55
00:03:21,830 --> 00:03:24,487
The moment you add a second parameter,

56
00:03:24,487 --> 00:03:28,962
every link that builds a query string has to carry both of them.

57
00:03:28,962 --> 00:03:32,739
Pass the tag back to the template, put it in the link,

58
00:03:32,739 --> 00:03:35,396
and older now goes to page two of two.

59
00:03:36,196 --> 00:03:38,389
And one small fix on the way.

60
00:03:38,389 --> 00:03:42,018
The tag list inside each post is a list as well,

61
00:03:42,018 --> 00:03:46,706
so the post row's border and padding landed on every tag pill.

62
00:03:46,706 --> 00:03:50,638
One child selector instead of a descendant selector.

63
00:03:51,438 --> 00:03:52,671
And here it is.

64
00:03:52,671 --> 00:03:58,920
The team, on the About page, in the order set by dragging rows in the admin.

65
00:03:59,720 --> 00:04:05,594
A testimonial on the home page, chosen by the editor from the snippet list.

66
00:04:06,394 --> 00:04:13,060
And the journal, filtered by tag, with every post showing its own tags as links.

67
00:04:13,860 --> 00:04:16,374
Commit, and tag.

68
00:04:17,174 --> 00:04:19,154
Next episode, navigation.

69
00:04:19,154 --> 00:04:21,689
A menu built from the page tree,

70
00:04:21,689 --> 00:04:26,600
and footer and contact details the client can edit themselves.

71
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:33,679
Next episode, navigation and site settings.

72
00:04:33,679 --> 00:04:36,600
Thanks for watching.
